    "body": "In module state mode looking up the module state is usually pretty slow (especially from utility code, where we mostly have to use the fallback mechanism). Therefore, it's good to avoid it as much as possible.\n\nWe can often use `Py_tp_token` to get quicker access to a token that lets us check type equality, or\n`PyType_GetBaseByToken` to get quicker access to the base class. This turns out to be ~3-5x faster than getting the module state (looking at microbenchmarks to the typecheck/`__Pyx_as_CyFunctionObject` functions.\n\nHowever, these can both fail in cases where cyfunction is a shared type that comes from a different module. Therefore I've distinguished between optimizations and cases where false negatives are a problem.\n\nI haven't applied this to the coroutine code since that's too much of a mix of optimizations and places where it's required to be right (and I suspect there's some hidden existing bugs lurking there...)",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
