                "message": "Faster module-state type checks for CyFunction\n\nIn module state mode looking up the module state is usually\npretty slow (especially from utility code, where we mostly\nhave to use the fallback mechanism). Therefore, it's good to\navoid it as much as possible.\n\nWe can often use `Py_tp_token` to get quicker access to a\ntoken that lets us check type equality, or\n`PyType_GetBaseByToken` to get quicker access to the base\nclass. This turns out to be ~3-5x faster than getting\nthe module state (looking at microbenchmarks to the\ntypecheck/`__Pyx_as_CyFunctionObject` functions.\n\nHowever, these can both fail in cases where cyfunction is\na shared type that comes from a different module. Therefore\nI've distinguished between optimizations and cases where false\nnegatives are a problem.\n\nI haven't applied this to the coroutine code since that's too much\nof a mix of optimizations and places where it's required to be right\n(and I suspect there's some hidden existing bugs lurking there...)",
